# Crossroads go every 27 cells, so the streets make a grid of squares. The
# third street runs into the main street, where its plot is free, and closes
# a loop with a crossroads.
> new empty
> free on
> construction off
> expect cannot build crossroads at s0:40 every 27 cells
  ok: can't build intersection at s0:40: Crossroads go only every 27 cells
> build crossroads at s0:55
  #1 intersection at s0:55-57, done
> ride #last
  rider: s0:56 facing +
> turn up
  rider: s1:131 facing +
> expect cannot build crossroads at s1:151 every 27 cells
  ok: can't build intersection at s1:151: Crossroads go only every 27 cells
> ride +27
  rider: s1:158 facing +
> build crossroads here
  #61 intersection at s1:157-159, done
> ride #last
  rider: s1:158 facing +
> turn up
  rider: s2:131 facing +
> ride +27
  rider: s2:158 facing +
> build crossroads here
  #97 intersection at s2:157-159, done
> expect streets 4
  ok: 4 streets
# three built, one made where the third street met the main street
> expect count crossroads 4
  ok: 4 intersection
> streets
  s0  runs east (lots on its north side), cells 10..252
  s1  runs north (lots on its west side), cells 10..252, from crossroads #1
  s2  runs west (lots on its south side), cells 10..252, from crossroads #61
  s3  runs south (lots on its east side), cells 10..252, from crossroads #97
    crossroads #1: s0:56 = s1:131 (cell A56)
    crossroads #61: s1:158 = s2:131 (cell AB56)
    crossroads #97: s2:158 = s3:131 (cell AB29)
    crossroads #98: s0:29 = s3:158 (cell A29)
